ted tracking mountain  lions in 2002 18 have died trying to  cross freeways and other secondary roads  without the overpass animals have been  forced to take risks or get created  Mountain Lion was it that made it  through here so it was p60 for this  image captured P 64 coming out of a  drainage pipe last year found this long  dark tunnel that unfortunately isn't  great in terms of a wildlife crossing in  general so far the National Wildlife  Federation has raised more than 13  million dollars from private donors and  they're confident they'll raise the  remaining 50 to 60 million completion is  set for 2023 so this is a pretty large  area how do we know that animals will  find their way to this one tiny bridge  so we put up a sign crossing that way no  you know what's great about wildlife  crossings is the science is really well  established where we have the advantage  from some of these other crossings is  this as it they're already trying to  cross here what I love about it too  we're saving mount lines we're  reconnecting an ecosystem but we're  gonna inspire the world that many people  are gonna drive under this and know  what's possible in LA if la can do it  nobody else has an excuse for CBS this  morning Carter Evans Agoura Hills  California
 

